[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Whether the six non-narrative types gain TAGS so a node can name a system by hand

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[DECISION]
UID: DEC-SYSTEM-TAG-ON-EVERY-ELEMENT
TITLE: Whether the six non-narrative types gain TAGS so a node can name a system by hand
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATUS: open
RETIRES_ON: A node needs to belong to a system its type does not place it in -- the first tooling mechanism that is really beads' -- and the beads import lands.
STATEMENT: >>>
Membership in a system is computed from a node's type (DEC-SYSTEM-IS-A-TYPE-
SET). A node whose type puts it in one system but which belongs to another
-- a tooling mechanism that is really part of the future beads engine -- has
no way to say so. A TAGS field on the other six types, carrying a token like
system/beads, would let it. Appending the field is free today; every
existing entry is a placeholder. But TAGS would enter those types' contract
hash unless excluded, and excluding it is one more constant in a script that
DEC-FP-FIELDS-CONFIGURABLE says should be an option. Open until the beads
import makes the need concrete.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Deciding it now would design beads ahead of its import, which the operator ruled out.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Opened 2026-08-30.
<<<
